        "message": "phases 1-5 complete: search, scoring, normalisation, geocoding, cross-corpus, dashboard upgrade\n\nSix-phase analysis pipeline now functional end-to-end (phase 0 OCR\nrunning in background, will land in subsequent commits as it completes).\n\nPhase 2b — Entity normalisation\n  extract/normalise-entities.mjs  Levenshtein-clustered dedup per\n                                  type. 159 raw case_numbers → 43\n                                  canonical; 87 raw classifications\n                                  → 18; AARO (2 spelling variants)\n                                  merged. Top recurring entities:\n                                  Richard A. Harrison (20 docs),\n                                  USCENTCOM (25), AARO (26), 609 CAOC\n                                  (19), USCENTCOM MDR 26-0019 (13).\n\nPhase 3b — Scoring with normalised entities\n  Top doc by composite: DOW-UAP-D25 Greece Jan 2024 (7.3).\n  Pattern: top 10 are all DoW Mission Reports across CENTCOM\n  theatre — Greece, Arabian Gulf, Iraq, Gulf of Aden, Strait of\n  Hormuz, Iran, Syria, UAE.\n\nPhase 4b — Dashboard upgrade\n  dashboard/index.html  6-view SPA with:\n  - corpus list with composite-score sort, agency filter, BM25-style\n    substring search, click-through entity filter\n  - inline PDF viewer (Mozilla pdf.js) on detail panel\n  - 6-axis scoring fingerprint visualisation\n  - map view (Leaflet, dark cartocdn tiles, geocoded incidents)\n  - timeline view (year-bucket bar chart + per-year doc list)\n  - entity drill-down view (sortable table by doc count, click → corpus filter)\n  - hypothesis register view with stance verdicts + evidence cards\n  - cross-corpus diff view (markdown render)\n\nPhase 4c — Geocoding\n  extract/geocode-locations.mjs  Nominatim lookup of unique\n                                 incident_location values. 8 of 8\n                                 locations resolved; \"Moon\" amusingly\n                                 resolves to Muhu, Estonia (expected\n                                 nominatim heuristic — kept for honesty).\n\nPhase 5b — Cross-corpus diff (H10 evidence)\n  extract/cross-corpus-diff.mjs  Compares war.gov/UFO/ Release 01\n                                 (115 sha256s) vs the on-disk noise\n                                 crawl (1408 sha256s from AARO.mil,\n                                 vault.fbi.gov, cia.gov, science.nasa.gov,\n                                 catalog.archives.gov, media.defense.gov,\n                                 captured earlier).\n  Key findings:\n    - 0 byte-identical matches: war.gov re-redacted/re-scanned\n      EVERYTHING. Not a single recycled blob.\n    - 8 AARO case-resolution PDFs publicly available but NOT in\n      war.gov/UFO/ — possible deliberate omissions.\n    - 32 FBI Vault UFO parts not mirrored despite the CSV claim of\n      \"complete case file with newly declassified pages\".\n  Output: extract/cross-corpus.jsonl + docs/cross-corpus-diff.md.\n\nGitHub Pages\n  .github/workflows/pages.yml  deploys dashboard + small JSON manifests\n                               + extracted text on every master push\n                               that touches relevant paths. Site URL:\n                               omgitzyeoku-collab.github.io/UFO/\n\nOCR pipeline (Phase 0a)\n  extract/ocr-pipeline.mjs  pymupdf renders each page → tesseract.js\n                            (WASM) does OCR. ~1 hour for 290-page\n                            FBI vault section. Running in background\n                            now; subsequent commits will land OCR\n                            text for all 65 scanned PDFs as they\n                            complete.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
